  "poseParity": "Exact across all four runs for time, steps, centers, velocities, rebuilt GPU vertices, all full hair vertices, head matrix, full body positions, rig, contact frames and camera. Each draw-only A/B restored these values exactly.",
  "method": "Actual production g050 Avatar at 4 s (481 solver steps), original 496 solved cards read back once, widths interpolated into camera-facing bundles. All 1128 cap triangles retained. Four views each for three variants; same full pose. No live follower simulation.",
  "observations": [
    "First 11904-strand constant-density pilot under-covered the wide fringe and changed the rest-local lock-albedo coordinate basis. It is rejected as final.",
    "Density control uses 31050 bundles at at most 0.6 mm center spacing at each source card widest ring and correct rest-local lock albedo. This changed two things, so it is not an isolated density or albedo mechanism test.",
    "Both early variants incorrectly placed coverage times atlas alpha only in opacityNode. Beauty saw it; HairOIT shadowCoverageMask and renderer shadow override ignored it and cast solid strips. This is a prototype bug, not a newly introduced production defect.",
    "Corrected variant places the product in colorNode.a and leaves opacityNode null. It retains all other density geometry and shader choices. Sides and rear read more continuous; root/crown patchwork and awkward separated hem strips remain. No final look adoption.",
    "Temporarily hiding all cap triangles in the density control did not remove the perceived broad upper patches. The patches cannot be attributed solely to the cap."
  ],
