  "limits": [
    "Coverage is resampled from the authored atlas, not mathematically preserved; copied lock IDs are dormant under geometric:true.",
    "Each 1.2 mm bundle extends beyond its source line, and inter-ring interpolated surfaces can differ from original triangles. Existing card collision guarantees do not transfer.",
    "Static follower geometry uses held velocity. It does not prove live deformation or camera-facing temporal vectors.",
    "All 496 cards are replaced in the render candidate, including protected roots, while production assets and solver state remain unchanged.",
    "Pilot Stage source preceded the separate viewport-size fix; its exact bytes are archived. Density and corrected coverage share the newer Stage source.",
    "Raw source and GLB hashes are frozen, but three visual runs did not save transformed served shader-module bytes. The cost run records its single timestamp-only Stage route.",
    "This is a render-primitive/tangent/coverage experiment, not an isolated lighting proof or an AAA-quality result."
  ],
  "next": "A scratch shader-gather prototype may test moving followers from the existing final card-edge GPU buffer, with no new guide simulation. Requires borrowed-buffer lifetime, correct coordinate basis, finite tangents, temporal limits, physical parity, visible motion, boundary clearance and cost gates."
